An attribute's name and a block's type and labels are `key` fields, as an object element's key already is, so the
diff matcher pairs `ami = ...` by its name and `resource "aws_instance" "web" { ... }` by its type and labels: a
member's key is its name within its scope (packages/syntechs/src/diff/matcher.ts, memberName).

A file's top-level attributes and blocks are the root's own children, not one `body` node's, the way every other
grammar's top-level declarations are: an added top-level block then reads as one whole added declaration
(packages/engine/src/fragments.ts, topOrMember). A block's `body` stays. src/grammars/hcl/highlights.tm.scm tells
a top-level block's type from a nested one's by `config_file` instead of the `body` upstream's queries go by.

A number's exponent no longer needs a fraction before it: HCL's NumericLit is `decimal+ ("." decimal+)? (expmark
decimal+)?` (hashicorp/hcl hclsyntax/spec.md), and upstream read `1e10` as the number `1` and the name `e10`.

The scanner (packages/syntechs/src/grammars/hcl/scanner.ts, a port of upstream's src/scanner.c) departs from
upstream in two places: it keeps a heredoc's state whatever its identifier's length or the nesting depth, where
upstream drops it past 127 and turns the rest of the file into errors, and it keeps the identifier's code points
whole, where upstream truncates each to a `char` and a non-ASCII identifier never finds its closing line.

An escape is an `escape_sequence` node of its own, a sibling of the `template_literal`s around it, so the highlight
can mark it `constant.character.escape`: in a quoted string `\n`, `\r`, `\t`, `\"`, `\\`, `\uXXXX` and
`\UXXXXXXXX`, and in a quoted string or a heredoc `$${` and `%%{`, which spell a literal `${` and `%{` (hashicorp/hcl
hclsyntax/spec.md). A heredoc reads a backslash as itself. scanner.ts emits the new token; src/scanner.c stays
upstream's, as for the heredoc departures above, and still folds an escape into the literal. A
`template_literal` keeps holding no named child, so a changed string run still diffs as one leaf and gets a word
diff (packages/syntechs/src/diff/content.ts, isContentAtom). A `string_lit` takes no escape, since a second
literal-or-escape rule there conflicts with `quoted_template`; a string with an escape is a `quoted_template`
instead, which a block label may now also be (`"a\tb"`), and the label queries match it too.

